From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrey Kasaurov <andrey.kasaurov@amd.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 01:45:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [AMDGPU] Don't emit EXEC-pair CFI for a single-subregister
 EXEC

llvm/llvm-project#213115 replaced the `NumSubRegs == 1` guard in
PrologEpilogSGPRSpillBuilder::copyToScratchSGPR with a check that both DWARF
register numbers are usable. Those two conditions differ on wave32: EXEC_LO is
a single 32-bit subregister, and findUnusedRegister can return a member of
SReg_32_XM0_XEXEC that has no DWARF encoding (everything in that class other
than SGPR_32 inherits the SIRegLoHi16 default of [-1, -1]). Such a save now
falls into the EXEC branch, whose assert requires a 64-bit EXEC pair, and
gfx1010 RCCL device code aborts the compiler on 24 objects:

  SIFrameLowering.cpp:426: PrologEpilogSGPRSpillBuilder::copyToScratchSGPR:
  Assertion `NumSubRegs == 2 && "EXEC larger than 64-bit"' failed.

With assertions disabled the same path is worse but silent:
buildCFIForRegToSGPRPairSpill asks a 32-bit register for sub0 and sub1, gets
NoRegister for both, and emits a .cfi_llvm_register_pair naming DWARF register
-1 twice.

Restrict the EXEC branch to the 64-bit pair it was written for and give the
single-subregister case its own arm. Note that simply adding `NumSubRegs == 2`
is not sufficient: the remaining per-subregister loop indexes SplitParts and
DstSplitParts, which are both empty when NumSubRegs == 1, so wave32 must not
reach it.

This is a local carry to unblock the comm-libs build with LLVM assertions
enabled (ROCm/TheRock#6102). Drop it once an upstream fix lands.
---
 {a => b}/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFrameLowering.cpp | 11 +++++++++--
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFrameLowering.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFrameLowering.cpp
index c258b99..49e73a2 100644
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFrameLowering.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFrameLowering.cpp
@@ -422,9 +422,16 @@ class PrologEpilogSGPRSpillBuilder {
         TFI->buildCFI(MBB, MI, DL,
                       MCCFIInstruction::createRegister(
                           nullptr, DwarfCFISuperReg, DwarfDstSuperReg));
-      } else if (isExec(CFISuperReg)) {
-        assert(NumSubRegs == 2 && "EXEC larger than 64-bit");
+      } else if (isExec(CFISuperReg) && NumSubRegs == 2) {
         TFI->buildCFIForRegToSGPRPairSpill(MBB, MI, DL, CFISuperReg, DstReg);
+      } else if (NumSubRegs == 1) {
+        // The copy destination has no DWARF register number. On wave32,
+        // findUnusedRegister can return a member of SReg_32_XM0_XEXEC that
+        // carries no DWARF encoding, and EXEC_LO is a single subregister, so
+        // neither the EXEC pair helper above nor the per-subregister loop
+        // below applies: SplitParts and DstSplitParts are both empty here.
+        // Describe nothing rather than naming DWARF register -1. The matching
+        // copyFromScratchSGPR emits no CFI either, so this stays balanced.
       } else {
         for (unsigned I = 0; I < NumSubRegs; ++I) {
           MCRegister SrcSubReg = TRI.getSubReg(SuperReg, SplitParts[I]);
-- 
